 exact env-var default already exists at `_dc_support.py:27`, whose own comment documents the codebase convention of re-reading `JIRA_DC_BASE_URL` with the same default so copies cannot drift. Since `_dc_fixtures.py` will already import from `_dc_support`, `from _dc_support import BASE` is a simpler, more codebase-aligned way to feed the extracted fixtures than adding a new fixture and rewiring the fixture graph.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7711c5d6e916ba30","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan', 4th bullet ('Thread the base URL through the fixture graph...')","norm_id":"nf74cf40e5b5656d9","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","scenarios":["Implementer adds a session-scoped fixture + rewires dc_transport/dc_store_copy_repo to depend on it, expanding the moved surface, when a one-line import from an already-imported module would suffice and match existing precedent."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In `_dc_fixtures.py`, add `BASE` to the existing `from _dc_support import ...` and use it in the extracted fixtures, dropping the `jira_dc_base_url` fixture entirely; note that this reuses the codebase's documented same-default anti-drift convention rather than introducing a third mechanism.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale